{# goal: Draft questions or grade actual identified answers, with deterministic feedback between executions and no generated bookkeeping. #}
[inference]
contract:
  input:
    topic: string
    phase: string
    mode: string
    current_level: integer
    round_number: integer
    question_bank: array
    answer_ids: array
    feedback: object
  output:
    question_drafts: array
    retired_explanations: array
    evaluations: array
    calibrated_level: integer|null
---
Examine **{{ topic }}**, batch {{ round_number }}, level {{ current_level }}, mode {{ mode }}.
Local ladder: 1 Recall; 2 Mechanism; 3 Rationale/tradeoffs; 4 Edge cases; 5 Synthesis.
This adapts Bloom; it is not the revised taxonomy's six categories.


{% if phase not in ["ask", "grade"] or mode not in ["calibrate", "interrogate"] %}
invalid_phase_or_mode — stop.
{% elif phase == "grade" %}
## Grade Identified Answers Only
Selected actual answers (a regrade keeps the same answer ID):
{% for answer in feedback.answers if answer.id in answer_ids %}
{% set question = question_bank | selectattr("id", "equalto", answer.question_id) | first %}
{{ {"answer": answer, "question": question} | tojson }}
{% endfor %}
Grade each selected answer Solid, Partial or Gap, with an answer-specific reason.
Return `{"evaluations":[{"answer_id":7,"rating":"Solid","note":"reason"}]}`;
the example ID is schematic: use only the supplied IDs, in any order.
Do not generate questions, answers, counters or a running assessment.
An empty selection is `no_answers_to_grade`, not permission to invent evidence.
{% if mode == "calibrate" %}
Also return `calibrated_level` (integer 1–5) based on these actual answers.
{% else %}
Omit `calibrated_level`; the caller supplies null to the update.
{% endif %}
{% elif feedback.stop or feedback.direction == "await_grades" or answer_ids | length > 0 %}
ask_blocked — finish grading or assess; do not generate questions.
{% else %}
## Draft Next Questions Only
Question bank: {{ question_bank | tojson }}
Feedback: {{ feedback.direction }}; retired IDs: {{ feedback.retired_ids | tojson }}.
Draft 2–3 questions at the supplied level. Hold probes deeper; reprobe changes angle;
escalate uses the already-raised level. Calibration asks baseline questions, not grades.
Return `question_drafts`: new `{retry_id:null,question,area}` records, or
`{retry_id:<original bank ID>,question:null,area:null}` for a legitimate retry.
The caller's delivery filter assigns new IDs and restores original retry records.
For every feedback.retired_ids entry return one `{question_id,explanation}` in
`retired_explanations`, explaining the correct answer instead of re-asking it.
Do not disguise a retired question as a new ID/paraphrase. If none are retired,
omit the explanation field; the caller retains the known empty set directly.
No assessment copy, level, ratio, counter or gate decision belongs in ask output.
{% endif %}

Stay within the topic; direct and challenging, never mean-spirited. Give minimal
hints without solving an active question. Grades use exact Solid/Partial/Gap casing.
